<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a DPDP compliance score?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A DPDP compliance score is a 0–100 rating indicating how well your business meets its obligations under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and DPDP Rules, 2025. Scores of 80–100 indicate strong compliance (low risk); 55–79 partial compliance (medium risk); 30–54 at risk (high risk); 0–29 non-compliant (critical risk)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is the DPDP compliance score calculated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The score is calculated from 20 questions across 6 DPDP obligation categories. Each answer scores Yes (2 pts), Partially (1 pt), or No (0 pts). Three questions covering the highest-penalty obligations are double-weighted: Privacy Policy, Consent mechanism, and Data Security). Raw score out of 44 is normalised to 100."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the DPDP Act penalties for non-compliance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"₹250 crore for security failures ; ₹200 crore for breach notification failure within 72 hours ; ₹200 crore for processing children's data without parental consent ; ₹50 crore each for no privacy policy, processing without consent, no Grievance Officer, retaining data beyond purpose, or ignoring erasure requests."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What changed in the DPDP Rules 2025?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The DPDP Rules 2025, notified November 13, 2025, add: (1) 1-year minimum retention of processing logs for all Data Fiduciaries (Rule 6 & 8); (2) 48-hour advance notice before deleting data for large platforms (Rule 8); (3) Grievance resolution must complete within 90 days (Rule 9); (4) Every personal data breach triggers notification to DPBI within 72 hours — no risk threshold (Rule 7); (5) Consent notice must be standalone and independent of any other document (Rule 3); (6) Verifiable parental consent via age/identity verification systems including DigiLocker (Rule 10)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When does DPDP compliance become mandatory?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Core provisions commenced November 13, 2025. Remaining provisions including Rules 3, 5–16, 22–23 take effect May 13, 2027 (18 months from Rules notification). Businesses should achieve full compliance before May 2027."}}]}</script>
